{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Young lions</b> — Some say: those who deny the fundamental principle. But the correct view in my eyes: they are human beings who resemble young lions in tearing prey in their gluttony — their violence and their hunger." "<b>Those who seek YHWH</b> — that they do not seek bread except from HaShem alone. Some say: when the men of Achish seized him they starved him, and as he stood before Achish he was hungry, and HaShem in His kindness helped him, like the way of Elijah."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:28.498352971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}